    "dram_protocol_efficiency": 1.0,
    "dram_protocol_efficiency_l1cached": 1.0,
    "derivation": "The A800 contract keeps both efficiencies at 1.0 because the sustained capacity is itself a measured stream rate that already contains protocol overhead, and .cg and .ca streams achieve the same rate.  On H200 .ca/.cg stays within the listed maximum deviation at every active-SM point, so both remain 1.0 relative to the measured read capacity above.  One CTA per SM (even at 1024 threads) does not saturate HBM3e, so this probe supplies the .cg/.ca ratio and dram_read_bw.cu supplies the capacity."
  },
